<script>
import bunfigSource from 'crm/bunfig.toml' with { type: 'text' }
import ClosedTiles from 'crm/src/reports/lib/ClosedTiles.abide'
import closedTilesSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/ClosedTiles.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import closedTilesTestSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/ClosedTiles.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import closedTotalsSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/closedTotals.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A test mounts a component and counts what a click did">
        <Example
            id="range-switch"
            app="crm"
            title="`mount(component)` and `measure(body)` — the DOM calls one click made"
            summary="The closed-deals tiles total the last 7 or 30 days. Its test switches the range and asserts that two numbers changed and nothing was built."
            files={{
                'src/reports/lib/ClosedTiles.abide': closedTilesSource,
                'src/reports/lib/closedTotals.ts': closedTotalsSource,
                'src/reports/lib/ClosedTiles.test.ts': closedTilesTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <ClosedTiles />
        </Example>

        <p><code>mount</code> renders the component the way the server does and hydrates it with
            the module the browser loads, so the test clicks the listener a reader clicks. It hands
            back a <code>Mounted</code>, and <code>using</code> stops it when the test ends.</p>

        <p><code>measure</code> counts every DOM call its body makes. A version that rebuilt the
            tiles shows the same numbers on screen and fails on <code>nodesCreated</code>. The one from
            <code>@abide/harness/abide</code> hands back an <code>AbideWork</code>: the DOM counts, plus
            <code>wakes</code>, <code>bindingRuns</code> and <code>descents</code> from abide itself.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Row of a <code>Work</code></th><th>Counts</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>nodesCreated</code></td><td><code>create*</code>, <code>cloneNode</code> and <code>importNode</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>elementsMoved</code></td><td>elements inserted or moved, with their subtrees</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>markersMoved</code> · <code>textMoved</code></td><td>comment and text nodes inserted or moved</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dataWrites</code> · <code>redundantDataWrites</code></td><td>text written, and text written over the same text</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>attributesSet</code></td><td>attributes set, removed or toggled</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>classWrites</code> · <code>styleWrites</code></td><td><code>classList</code> changes, and inline style writes</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>listenersBound</code></td><td><code>addEventListener</code> calls</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>published</code></td><td>what code on the page counted itself</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>A DOM member the harness does not count throws while a case is open, rather than
            reading as zero. <code>patchSet()</code> lists every member it does count.</p>

        <p>The DOM under <code>bun test</code> comes from the <code>preload</code> line in
            <code>bunfig.toml</code>, which the scaffold writes:</p>

        <Snippet source={bunfigSource} path="bunfig.toml" from={['[test]', 'preload =']} />

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Preload</th><th>What it gives a test</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>preload = ["@abide/harness/abide/preload"]</code></td><td>a counted DOM, <code>.abide</code> imports as components, and <code>mount</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>preload = ["@abide/abide/test"]</code></td><td><code>.abide</code> imports as components, for a test that only renders</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>preload = ["@abide/harness/preload"]</code></td><td>a counted DOM alone, for code that is not abide</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>The emulated DOM is JavaScript, so a count from it holds in a browser and a millisecond
            does not. Count under <code>bun test</code>, and time in a bench. The DOM counts alone come
            from <code>@abide/harness/measure</code> › <code>measure</code>, which hands back a plain
            <code>Work</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
